+#### [PyCaret](https://github.com/pycaret/pycaret)
+> **Description:** PyCaret is a low-code machine-learning library that automates end-to-end experiment workflows across classification, regression, anomaly detection, clustering, and time series. Hotels can use it to prototype demand models, churn or cancellation models, review classification, lead scoring, or operational anomaly detection without building every pipeline manually. The README is candid about its goal: replace a large amount of repetitive ML boilerplate with a few lines of Python while still exposing common libraries under the hood. For hotel analytics teams that want faster experimentation, it remains a practical OSS option. GitHub metadata: last commit **2025-04-21**, **9.6k** stars, primary language **Jupyter Notebook**, license **MIT**.
