+# Best AI Tools for Hotels in 2026
+
+[![Awesome](https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/sindresorhus/awesome@main/media/badge.svg)](https://github.com/sindresorhus/awesome)
+[![License: MIT](https://img.shields.io/badge/License-MIT-yellow.svg)](https://opensource.org/licenses/MIT)
+![Topics](https://img.shields.io/github/stars/GagnDeep/awesome-best-ai-tools-for-hotels-2026?style=social)
+
+> Best AI tools for hotels in 2026 are mostly open-source building blocks rather than hotel-only products. This list curates verified GitHub repositories that hotels can self-host for concierge chat, guest messaging, voice automation, document extraction, booking knowledge search, and demand forecasting, while being honest about the gaps in hotel-native OSS.
+
+## Table of Contents
+- [TL;DR](#tldr)
+- [Why This List](#why-this-list)
+- [Open Source Tools](#open-source-tools)
+- [FAQ](#faq)
+- [Contributing](#contributing)
+- [License](#license)
+
+## TL;DR
+- **Best all-around concierge stack:** [RasaHQ/rasa](https://github.com/RasaHQ/rasa), [FlowiseAI/Flowise](https://github.com/FlowiseAI/Flowise), and [langflow-ai/langflow](https://github.com/langflow-ai/langflow) for multi-step guest support and booking-assistant flows.
+- **Best self-hosted knowledge and document stack:** [Mintplex-Labs/anything-llm](https://github.com/Mintplex-Labs/anything-llm), [docling-project/docling](https://github.com/docling-project/docling), and [OCRmyPDF/OCRmyPDF](https://github.com/OCRmyPDF/OCRmyPDF) for SOPs, policies, menus, PDFs, and scanned forms.
+- **Best voice stack for hotels:** [pipecat-ai/pipecat](https://github.com/pipecat-ai/pipecat), [livekit/agents](https://github.com/livekit/agents), [SYSTRAN/faster-whisper](https://github.com/SYSTRAN/faster-whisper), and [rhasspy/piper](https://github.com/rhasspy/piper) for phone, kiosk, and in-room assistants.
+- **Best local/private inference stack:** [BerriAI/litellm](https://github.com/BerriAI/litellm), [ollama/ollama](https://github.com/ollama/ollama), and [vllm-project/vllm](https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm) for routing, serving, and cost control.
+- **Best forecasting options for hotel demand planning:** [Nixtla/neuralforecast](https://github.com/Nixtla/neuralforecast), [Nixtla/statsforecast](https://github.com/Nixtla/statsforecast), [Nixtla/mlforecast](https://github.com/Nixtla/mlforecast), [Nixtla/hierarchicalforecast](https://github.com/Nixtla/hierarchicalforecast), and [pycaret/pycaret](https://github.com/pycaret/pycaret).
+
+## Why This List
+Hotels need AI that can be audited, customized, and deployed around sensitive guest data, call recordings, booking rules, rate plans, and property SOPs. Open source is especially valuable here because it lets hotel teams self-host, integrate with PMS or CRM layers, avoid SaaS lock-in, and adapt workflows for concierge, reservations, front desk, housekeeping, revenue management, and guest communications.
+
+The hard truth: there are very few hotel-native open-source AI repositories on GitHub. The best AI tools for hotels in 2026 are mostly general-purpose OSS systems that can be adapted to hospitality operations. This list favors tools with active repositories, clear licenses, and obvious hotel use cases over weak keyword matches.
+
