+# Contributing
+
+Thanks for contributing to `awesome-best-ai-tools-for-hotels-2026`.
+
+## Submission Rules
+
+To keep this repository useful and defensible:
+
+1. Every tool **must** have a public `github.com` repository URL.
+2. No proprietary SaaS-only products.
+3. Prefer OSI-approved open-source licenses.
+4. If a project is source-available with meaningful restrictions, mention that clearly in the PR.
+5. Every submission must explain why the tool is relevant to hotels, not just why it is a good AI repo in general.
+
+## Required Data For Each Submission
+
+Please include:
+
+- Repository name
+- GitHub URL
+- Short description based on the project README
+- Star count
+- Primary language
+- License
+- Last commit date
+- Suggested category
+- Best hotel use case
+
+## Preferred Pull Request Format
+
+Use this template in your PR description:
+
+```md
+## Repository
+- Name:
+- GitHub URL:
+
+## Metadata
+- Stars:
+- Language:
+- License:
+- Last Commit:
+
+## Why It Belongs
+- Hotel use case:
+- Why it is better than similar repos:
+
+## Notes
+- License caveats:
+- Maintenance caveats:
+```
+
+## Quality Bar
+
+PRs may be closed if they:
+
+- add tools without a GitHub repo
+- add repos that are clearly unrelated to hospitality use cases
+- omit metadata
+- use vague marketing copy instead of README-based descriptions
+- hide licensing ambiguity
+
+## Style
+
+- Keep descriptions concise and factual.
+- Prefer GitHub-verified metadata.
+- Be honest about category gaps. Do not pad the list with weak matches just to increase the count.
+
+## License
+
+By contributing, you agree that your contributions will be licensed under the MIT License used by this repository.
