+> **Description:** LlamaIndex describes itself as a leading framework for building LLM-powered agents over your data, with both high-level APIs and lower-level control over ingestion, retrievers, query engines, and rerankers. That flexibility is valuable for hotel teams that want to start with a basic property knowledge assistant and later evolve toward richer booking, concierge, or revenue copilots. The README is especially strong on connecting your own data sources to production-ready agent behavior rather than just raw chat. Because it is MIT licensed and highly adopted, it fits well as a backbone library inside a hotel AI stack. GitHub metadata: last commit **2026-01-08**, **46.2k** stars, primary language **Python**, license **MIT**.
