+### Voice & Call Automation
+
+#### [Pipecat](https://github.com/pipecat-ai/pipecat)
+> **Description:** Pipecat is an open-source framework for real-time voice and multimodal conversational agents. Its README is unusually concrete about the target workloads: speech-to-text, text-to-speech, transport layers, analytics, and pluggable AI services for ultra-low-latency interaction. That is directly relevant to hotel call automation, front-desk voice assistants, smart lobby kiosks, and guest-support phone flows. Pipecat’s architecture is more composable than turnkey, so it fits best when a hotel engineering team wants full control of telephony, voice UX, and orchestration rather than a hosted call-center product. GitHub metadata: last commit **2026-01-05**, **9.6k** stars, primary language **Python**, license **BSD-2-Clause**.
